C5 — midnight-pin semantics. PASS with a reported, sub-0.2% arithmetic delta.
  Preview and apply both call the same computeDashboardSync, so both use the
  same pinned `now` and the hash agrees — demonstrated by the happy path
  returning 200 (a differing `now` breaks it: mutant D above).
  Today's transactions: INCLUDED, both before and after the change. Probe
  zz_probe_test.go compares the OLD live end bound with the NEW pinned one on a
  fixture containing a today-dated outflow:
    OLD (time.Now)      : txns_in_window=25 months=11.156044459 NewMonthlyExpenses=2240.848008
    NEW (local midnight): txns_in_window=25 months=11.138888889 NewMonthlyExpenses=2244.299252
    delta txns=0  delta avg=3.451244  relative=0.154015%
    today-dated transaction included under the midnight pin: true
  So window MEMBERSHIP is unchanged (structurally too: both bounds land on the
  same calendar day, and FilterByDateRange normalises to that day's edges). The
  only semantic delta is the `months` divisor in the partial-history branch
  (`months = now.Sub(filtered.MinDate())/24/30`), which shrinks by up to one
  day, raising NewMonthlyExpenses by <=1day/months (0.154% on this fixture) and
  by exactly 0 when the data spans the full 12 months (months is the constant
  12.0 then). A second, same-magnitude effect: incomePatternStale's gapDays is
  now measured from midnight, so a pattern is up to 1 day "less stale" at the
  nominalDays*2+7 boundary. FINDING (C5, informational): a real but sub-0.2%,
  bounded-by-one-day change in the computed average in the partial-history case.
  It is not a silent regression in the ordinary sense — the OLD value was not
  reproducible at all (it drifted with sub-second wall-clock), which is the bug
  being fixed. Severity: below the acceptance criteria, which demand a stable
  hash, not identity with the old drifting average.
  SECOND FINDING (C5, cosmetic): the added Description sort REPLACES
  insights.IncomePatterns' TotalAmount-descending order, so the preview's
  "Income sources to add" / "Detected but not synced" lists now render
  alphabetically instead of largest-first. The top-10 truncation is unaffected
  (it happens inside IncomePatterns, before the re-sort). Evidence: probe log
  "first-run Added order: [Alpha Deposit Bravo Deposit Charlie Deposit Delta
  Deposit]" on a fixture whose insertion order is unrelated to that.

